# Copy to client/.env and fill in. Never commit the real .env.
#
# Everything with a VITE_ prefix is compiled into the JavaScript bundle and is
# readable by anyone who opens the site. That is expected for the Firebase web
# config, which is an identifier rather than a secret — access is controlled by
# firestore.rules and storage.rules, not by hiding these values.
#
# The OpenCage and Cloudinary values ARE billable, so restrict them in their
# respective dashboards (HTTP referrer allowlist / restricted upload preset).

# Firebase — Project settings > General > Your apps > SDK setup and configuration
# No storageBucket: Cloud Storage is not used (it requires the Blaze plan on new
# projects). All images go to Cloudinary.
VITE_API_KEY=
VITE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
VITE_PROJECT_ID=your-project
VITE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_APP_ID=

# OpenCage geocoding — https://opencagedata.com/dashboard
# Restrict to your production domain and set a daily request cap.
VITE_OPENCAGE_API_KEY=

# Cloudinary unsigned upload — Settings > Upload > Upload presets
# This is the ONLY image upload path in the app (listing photos and profile
# pictures both). The preset must be restricted: image-only, max 2 MB, allowed
# formats png/jpg/webp, and an allowed-origins list. An open unsigned preset
# lets anyone upload anything to your account, on your bill.
VITE_CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=
VITE_CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET=
